<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Communities (Digital Experiences) settings required by the Office Depot storefront.

  enableOotbProfExtUserOpsEnable is the metadata name of the Setup checkbox
  "Allow using standard external profiles for self-registration, user creation, and login"
  (Setup > Digital Experiences > Settings).

  Without it, creating an external buyer User on a STANDARD profile such as
  "Customer Community Plus User" fails with:
    FIELD_INTEGRITY_EXCEPTION - "To create or update users for this profile, go to Setup >
    Digital Experiences > Settings and select Allow using standard external profiles for
    self-registration, user creation, and login.: Profile ID"
  Observed against scratch org 00DG100000EKcgz on 2026-09-21, where the value defaults to false.
  The Developer Edition sandbox 00DgL00000L7NwjUAF already had it true, which is why its six
  buyer users could be created without hitting this.

  Capturing it here turns what the error message presents as a manual Setup-UI step into a
  deployable metadata change - it does NOT need to be done by hand.
-->
<CommunitiesSettings xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <enableNetworksEnabled>true</enableNetworksEnabled>
    <enableOotbProfExtUserOpsEnable>true</enableOotbProfExtUserOpsEnable>
</CommunitiesSettings>
